      "step_number": 4,
      "text": "Step 4: Since \\( a_{2k+2} \\) must also be part of a geometric sequence starting from \\( a_{2k+1} \\), we have:\n\\[ a_{2k+2} = a_{2k+1}r = a_{2k-1}r^2r = a_{2k-1}r^3 \\]\nEquating the two expressions for \\( a_{2k+2} \\):\n\\[ a_{2k-1}r^2(2 - \\frac{1}{r}) = a_{2k-1}r^3 \\]\n\\[ 2 - \\frac{1}{r} = r \\]\n\\[ 2r - 1 = r^2 \\]\n\\[ r^2 - 2r + 1 = 0 \\]\n\\[ (r-1)^2 = 0 \\]\n\\[ r = 1 \\]",
